Ship BLAST-ImpactX/impactx#1613 ahead of the next ImpactX release.

Windows upper-cases environment variable names and CMake variables are
case-sensitive, so the generic escape hatch
IMPACTX_CMAKE_ImpactX_openpmd_internal=OFF arrives as
-DIMPACTX_OPENPMD_INTERNAL=OFF and nothing reads it: the Windows wheels keep
ImpactX_openpmd_internal=ON and rebuild openPMD-api in-tree once per CPython,
on top of the external one library_builders.bat already built.

This adds the missing all-caps IMPACTX_OPENPMD_{INTERNAL,SRC,REPO,BRANCH}
variables (mirroring the AMReX/pyAMReX block, same ON default), which survive
Windows' upper-casing. Docs hunk dropped -- the wheel build does not need it.

Drop this once SRC_REF advances past a release containing impactx#1613.

